268
00:12:06,410 --> 00:12:08,110
Aw, that movie's so cute.

269
00:12:08,110 --> 00:12:10,140
Do you like her because you both have red hair?

270
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:12,740
Uh, a little, but more that she's covered in scars

271
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:15,730
and can pull her own limbs off and sew them back on.

272
00:12:17,650 --> 00:12:19,630
I like Cinderella.

273
00:12:21,890 --> 00:12:23,560
Did you know, in the original book,

274
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,540
the sisters cut off their toes with knives

275
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:27,800
in order to fit in the glass slipper?

276
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:31,570
I like "Bibbidi-Bobbidi-Boo."

277
00:12:33,010 --> 00:12:35,000
Hey, here comes Stuart and his date.

278
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,250
Oh, she's cute.

279
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:39,000
Oh, my God.

280
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:39,670
What?

281
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:40,930
That's Jeanie.

282
00:12:40,930 --> 00:12:42,220
That's Jeanie?!

283
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:43,410
- Who's Jeanie? - Don't say it.

284
00:12:43,410 --> 00:12:46,130
That's Howard's cousin that he had sex with.

285
00:12:49,190 --> 00:12:50,650
She is my second cousin.

286
00:12:50,650 --> 00:12:53,790
We were 15... I just said, "don't say it."

287
00:12:54,890 --> 00:12:55,930
No, it's okay.

288
00:12:55,930 --> 00:12:57,600
He told me that story a long time ago.

289
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,520
Raj!

290
00:12:58,520 --> 00:12:59,520
It was our first date,

291
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,670
there was an awkward silence.

292
00:13:00,670 --> 00:13:02,720
What was I supposed to say?

293
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:11,160
Oh, it's beautiful.

294
00:13:11,990 --> 00:13:13,680
Oh, the girls really did a nice job.

295
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:16,070
I know I wasn't into this before,

296
00:13:16,070 --> 00:13:19,050
but I'm so glad I get to take you to your first prom.

297
00:13:19,230 --> 00:13:21,040
What makes you think I didn't go to my prom?

298
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,960
- I went. - Well, who'd you go with?

299
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:27,110
I took a little lady I like to call loneliness.

300
00:13:28,650 --> 00:13:29,380
Aw, it's all right.

301
00:13:29,380 --> 00:13:30,860
We ended up having a threesome

302
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:32,690
with her friend humiliation, so...

303
00:13:35,350 --> 00:13:37,240
Well, if I would have been there and saw you alone,

304
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,390
I would've asked you to dance.

305
00:13:38,390 --> 00:13:39,410
No, you wouldn't have.

306
00:13:39,410 --> 00:13:40,470
Well, you don't know that.

307
00:13:40,470 --> 00:13:42,150
It was before my growth spurt.

308
00:13:42,150 --> 00:13:43,700
What, that already happened?

309
00:13:46,390 --> 00:13:47,330
Very funny.

310
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:48,790
Well, you wouldn't have asked me either.

311
00:13:48,790 --> 00:13:50,290
I would have asked you.

312
00:13:51,270 --> 00:13:52,690
In my head.

313
00:13:54,130 --> 00:13:55,670
On the way home.

314
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:58,640
While I was having a good cry.

315
00:14:05,070 --> 00:14:06,760
Sheldon, can I come in?

316
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:08,870
I don't think that's a good idea.

317
00:14:08,870 --> 00:14:10,180
Why not?

318
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:11,900
According to an online message board,

319
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:13,980
I may be having a panic attack.

320
00:14:13,980 --> 00:14:17,490
SoccerMom09 had similar symptoms.

321
00:14:18,310 --> 00:14:22,110
But to be fair, the twins were a real handful that day.

322
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,060
You're making me worry.

323
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:25,530
What's going on?

324
00:14:25,970 --> 00:14:29,170
What's going on is we're about to go to a prom.

325
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:30,680
And there's a great deal of pressure

326
00:14:30,680 --> 00:14:32,780
on young couples like us to engage in

327
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:36,160
what Mr. Bob Eubanks called making whoopee.

328
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:38,200
What pressure?

329
00:14:38,200 --> 00:14:39,930
All I said was you look handsome.

330
00:14:39,930 --> 00:14:41,900
Can you please open the door?

331
00:14:42,380 --> 00:14:44,370
It's not just that.

332
00:14:44,370 --> 00:14:47,220
Leonard and Penny also made comments about it.

333
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,810
And I'm not blind.

334
00:14:48,810 --> 00:14:51,170
Even I looked twice when I saw my posterior

335
00:14:51,170 --> 00:14:53,460
in these tuxedo pants.

336
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:58,020
So, I met Jeanie at your Aunt Gladys'.

337
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,490
She passed me the Manischewitz,

338
00:14:59,490 --> 00:15:01,140
I took one look at this punim,

339
00:15:01,140 --> 00:15:03,770
and I almost plotzed on the kugel.

340
00:15:06,700 --> 00:15:09,290
Is this what I sound like when I talk about India?

341
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:13,600
So, my mother's okay with this?

342
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:16,180
Why would your mother have a problem with me and Stuart?

343
00:15:16,180 --> 00:15:19,390
'Cause they have a weird, inappropriate relationship.

344
00:15:19,390 --> 00:15:22,930
Weirder than what you and I did in my dad's Corolla?

345
00:15:25,700 --> 00:15:27,260
This is so messed up.

346
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,700
I know, I'm having the best time.

347
00:15:31,150 --> 00:15:32,900
Why would you even come to this?

348
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:34,590
Didn't you know I'd be here?

349
00:15:34,590 --> 00:15:36,530
It was a long time ago, Howard.

350
00:15:36,530 --> 00:15:38,890
And you're only second cousins, who cares?

351
00:15:38,890 --> 00:15:41,360
So, you knew and you brought her anyway?

352
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:44,180
Oh, so she's good enough for Howard, but not for me?!

353
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:44,770
Yeah.

354
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:46,230
Yeah, go have weird relationships

355
00:15:46,230 --> 00:15:47,560
with your own mother and cousin.

356
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,440
This is his turf.

357
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,930
Yeah.

358
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,600
Well, I might not have asked you to dance then,

359
00:15:55,600 --> 00:15:58,460
- but I will ask you now. - There's no music.

360
00:15:58,460 --> 00:15:59,430
I don't care.

361
00:15:59,430 --> 00:16:01,060
We'll make our own music.

362
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:03,140
My God, who's the dork now?

363
00:16:11,030 --> 00:16:13,200
Thank you for wearing your flats.

364
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:15,890
Thank you for wearing your heels.

365
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:20,810
Look at me.

366
00:16:20,810 --> 00:16:24,030
Dancing with the prettiest girl at the prom.

367
00:16:24,550 --> 00:16:25,890
Want to take a picture of us and send it

368
00:16:25,890 --> 00:16:28,150
to your old friends in the chess club?

369
00:16:28,870 --> 00:16:31,910
I sent them a bikini shot of you years ago.

370
00:16:35,550 --> 00:16:37,120
This is nice.

371
00:16:37,810 --> 00:16:39,840
I kind of wish no one else was coming.

372
00:16:40,070 --> 00:16:42,110
I know, me, too.

373
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:46,300
But it will be fun to have a prom without all the drama.

374
00:16:49,210 --> 00:16:50,760
Howie, get off of him!

375
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:54,520
Not until he stops humping his way up my family tree!

376
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:58,510
Sheldon, this is silly.

377
00:16:58,510 --> 00:17:00,050
I'm not missing another prom.

378
00:17:00,050 --> 00:17:01,250
I'm going upstairs now.

379
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:02,670
Good-bye.

380
00:17:03,680 --> 00:17:06,250
I really did think you looked pretty.

381
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:07,920
You did?

382
00:17:08,370 --> 00:17:09,290
Yes.

383
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:12,800
So much so that I started to panic.

384
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,630
Well, you can relax.

385
00:17:15,320 --> 00:17:17,280
Just because you think I look pretty

386
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:21,040
doesn't mean we have to spend the night together.

387
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:24,230
Were you hoping we would because it's prom?

388
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:26,540
I'm always hoping.

389
00:17:27,570 --> 00:17:31,610
But tonight I just wanted to have a nice time with you.

390
00:17:32,030 --> 00:17:35,700
And maybe dance with someone who has arms.

391
00:17:37,030 --> 00:17:38,950
Thank you for understanding.

392
00:17:38,950 --> 00:17:41,220
Of course I understand.

393
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:44,730
Sheldon,

394
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,860
there's something else I've been wanting to say,

395
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:49,580
but before I do, I just...

396
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:53,320
I want you to know that you don't have to say it back.

397
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:54,580
I know you're not ready,

398
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:56,500
and I don't want you to say it

399
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,360
just because social convention dictates...

400
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:00,110
I love you, too.

401
00:18:04,670 --> 00:18:06,300
You said it.

402
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:08,630
There's no denying I have feelings for you

403
00:18:08,630 --> 00:18:11,220
that can't be explained in any other way.

404
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:16,040
I briefly considered that I had a brain parasite.

405
00:18:18,560 --> 00:18:20,690
But that seems even more farfetched.

406
00:18:24,150 --> 00:18:26,520
The only conclusion was love.

407
00:18:30,630 --> 00:18:32,420
I know what's happening.

408
00:18:33,930 --> 00:18:35,630
This is a panic attack.

409
00:18:35,630 --> 00:18:38,300
SoccerMom09 says to lie down with your feet elevated.

410
00:18:38,300 --> 00:18:39,680
Okay.

411
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:42,640
Just because I love you doesn't mean

412
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,950
girls are allowed in my room.

413
00:18:56,690 --> 00:18:58,120
Okay.

414
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:00,300
Here we go...

415
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:02,300
Say "Cheese"!

416
00:19:05,190 --> 00:19:07,040
Say "Cheese"!

417
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:13,080
Say "Cousin"!

418
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:17,210
Say...

419
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:19,110
Oh, sorry.

420
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:21,050
Hang on, sorry.

421
00:19:23,110 --> 00:19:24,560
Hey, Debbie.

422
00:19:25,070 --> 00:19:27,480
I... Yeah, yeah, I'm here with Jeanie.

423
00:19:28,050 --> 00:19:30,290
Okay, but we're just friends.

424
00:19:30,290 --> 00:19:32,400
It's... Yeah.

425
00:19:32,560 --> 00:19:33,680
I got to go.

